WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.037
Let’s bring the ideas together.

00:00:02.037 --> 00:00:04.692
Mean and median describe center.

00:00:04.692 --> 00:00:08.382
Range and standard deviation describe spread.

00:00:08.382 --> 00:00:11.492
Frequencies help describe a distribution.

00:00:11.492 --> 00:00:14.477
Grouped statistics support comparisons.

00:00:14.477 --> 00:00:22.207
Correlation describes linear association, and confidence intervals remind us that estimates contain uncertainty.

00:00:22.878 --> 00:00:29.403
Good visualization and reporting connect those statistics back to the question the audience actually cares about.

00:00:29.853 --> 00:00:36.835
Module 14 brings many of the course ideas together in an introductory machine learning workflow.

00:00:36.835 --> 00:00:45.175
We’ll read data, separate features from a target, create training and testing sets, train a simple model,

00:00:45.175 --> 00:00:52.125
evaluate its predictions, compare it with a baseline, and discuss issues such as data leakage and responsible

00:00:52.125 --> 00:00:54.186
interpretation.
